--
In a partial specialization over a function type (W<R(Args...)>), a
member taking the pack (Args... args) with a pack-expanded functional
cast `Args(args)...` in its body fails conversion ("found no match
for symbol 'Args'"; the argument list arrives empty at the cast) and
the member is left bodyless.  The plain variadic form W<Args...>
works.  Remaining layer of cpp17_function_handler_dispatch
(libstdc++ std::function::operator()).  g++/clang++/valgrind clean.
